# Trivy exceptions for this repository.
#
# The CVE gate blocks on any FIXABLE CRITICAL or HIGH (see the security scan
# job in .gitlab-ci.yml). This file is the sanctioned way to proceed when one
# of those genuinely cannot be taken right now -- and it exists because the
# alternative is real: a blocking gate with no exception path gets weakened
# the first time it is inconvenient, and a weakened gate still reads as
# protection while protecting nothing.
#
# It is deliberately empty. As of 2026-09-29 there are zero fixable CRITICAL
# or HIGH findings across all six repositories, so nothing needs excusing.
#
# RULES FOR AN ENTRY
#
#   1. One CVE per line, with a comment above it giving:
#        - why the fix cannot be taken now (not "it's noisy")
#        - what would have to change for it to be taken
#        - a REVIEW BY date, at most 90 days out
#   2. Never add a CVE here to unblock a merge you are in the middle of.
#      Raise it, decide it, then add it.
#   3. An entry past its review date is a finding in its own right.
#
# Note that an advisory with NO fix available never reaches this file: the
# scan runs with --ignore-unfixed, so it does not block anyone in the first
# place. Everything here is therefore something that COULD have been fixed
# and was consciously not.
#
# Example of the required shape:
#
#   # CVE-2026-00000 in example-lib 1.2.3, fixed in 2.0.0.
#   # 2.0.0 drops Node 20, which the field app still targets. Taking it means
#   # moving the Electron runtime first (tracked in P3.6).
#   # REVIEW BY: 2026-12-15
#   CVE-2026-00000
